plan_validation[1]{text,command,expected}:
  "Second exact-head review produced two useful maintainability findings: derive target selector keys from TargetOptions, share extraction payload construction across extract and related, and cover combined group expansion plus secondary topology. Implemented with no duplicate test case.","bun run test -- tests/websocket-command.test.ts; bun run typecheck; bun run lint; bun run quality:file-size; bun run test:coverage","22 focused tests and 1,407 total tests pass with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and source files remain within 300 code lines."
plan_decisions[1]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-08-09T21:30:24.486Z",codex-root,"Expose an affirmative --include-secondary flag while preserving Core's primary-only default; apply it to extract and related topology only, because triggers conditions and services do not accept primary_entities_only.","An affirmative opt-in is intuitive, prevents payload expansion by default, and maps exactly to primary_entities_only:false without inventing fallback behavior.",Tagged Core command schema and current CLI payload inspection
plan_discoveries[1]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T21:30:24.102Z",codex-root,Core 2026.8.1 is the latest release; commands.py defines primary_entities_only default true for extract_from_target. The live server is 2026.7.4 and the option was introduced in Core during the 2026.5 development cycle.
